{
	"_doc": [
		"Hand-made voxel models (the placeable picker's 'Claude' method), by block name.",
		"Built at the sprite's art resolution (Data art: one voxel per pixel of the original art), w x h pixels and w voxels deep; z runs 0 (back) to w - 1 (front).",
		"parts: the first part whose rect [x0, y0, x1, y1] (art pixels, inclusive, y down) holds an opaque pixel gives that pixel's column of voxels: z ranges [[z0, z1], ...] (inclusive). default: the same for pixels in no part. Transparent pixels get no voxels. match [x, y]: the part only takes pixels of that art pixel's colour (the dark gaps between books, drawer knobs).",
		"Seen from the front each column shows its front-most voxel, which always takes the sprite pixel's own colour, so the front view is the sprite. fill [x, y]: the art pixel whose colour the column's other voxels take (the top of a tabletop, the sides of a leg); without it they take their own pixel's colour (the sprite pushed back).",
		"shift: [[dx, dy], ...] per animation frame (looping): where the part, its rect and its match/fill pixels have moved to in that frame (the Extractinator's bobbing hopper)."
	],
